alic>&#x0003c;0.01.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>The Study Variables According to CAT Score</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-54-1214-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>CAT, COPD assessment test; COPD, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease; MRC, Medical Research Council; ANOVA, analysis variance; BMI, body mass index; SD, standart deviation; ns, not significant.</p><p>CAT I: mild; CAT II: moderate; CAT III: severe; CAT IV: very severe. All data represent mean (SD) except MRC dyspnea scale that show frequency (row percentage). ANOVA results (column 1).</p><p><sup>*</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.03.</p><p><sup>&#x02020;</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.003.</p><p><sup>&#x02021;</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.001.</p><p><sup>&#x000a7;</sup><italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.001.</p><p>Post-hoc Bonferroni test: vs. column 2; <sup>&#x02225;</sup><italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.001, vs. column 3; <sup>&#x000b6;</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.003, vs. column 4; <sup>**</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.007, <sup>&#x02020;&#x02020;</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.005, vs. column 5; <sup>&#x02021;&#x02021;</sup><italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.05, <sup>&#x000a7;&#x000a7;</sup><italic>p</italic>=0.001.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Difference in CAT Scores and between Classes of Other COPD Impairment Measures</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-54-1214-i004"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Ns, not significant; GOLD, Global Initiative Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease; MRC, Medical Research Council; COPD, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease; CAT, COPD assessment test; SD, standart deviation.</p><p>All data presented as mean (SD).</p><p><sup>*</sup>Differences among below scores.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>